# vNext - graphify Ignore Rules
#
# gitignore syntax. Merged with .gitignore (which already excludes bin/obj/.vs/
# node_modules/ai-docs/graphify-out etc.) — .gitignore is read first, this file
# last, so entries here only ever exclude MORE, never re-include anything.
#
# Everything below IS tracked in git but adds noise or near-zero relationship
# signal to the knowledge graph (auto-generated scaffolding, flat data blobs,
# dependency lockfiles) rather than being excluded for size/build reasons.

# EF Core migration scaffolding - auto-generated by `dotnet ef migrations add`,
# pure DbContext model-builder chains with no domain relationships. Also the
# single largest generated-code footprint in the repo (100+ files, ~2MB).
src/BBT.Workflow.Infrastructure/Migrations/**/*.Designer.cs
src/BBT.Workflow.Infrastructure/Migrations/**/*ModelSnapshot.cs

# Postman/Mockoon exports - flat request/response/mock-route JSON blobs, not
# source relationships.
docs/monitoring/endpoints/*.postman_collection.json
etc/docker/config/mockoon/*.json

# Dependency lockfiles - not meaningful graph nodes.
**/package-lock.json

# Explicit belt-and-suspenders excludes (already covered by .gitignore today,
# kept here so the graph stays clean even if .gitignore's coverage changes).
node_modules/
dist/
build/
bin/
obj/
*.min.js
*.generated.*
coverage/
test/**/fixtures/
tests/**/fixtures/
